Note that increasing a school from Skilled to Expert will *never* improve 
the fail rate of level three (and below) spells, *regardless* of class. 
Here's a quick spoiler.  Anyone who wants to is welcome to copy it.

 Spell Level     Basic        Skilled        Expert
---------------------------------------------------
      1          XL  3           -             -   
      2          XL 18           -             -   
      3            +           XL 15           -   
      4            +             +           XL 18 
      5            +             +           XL 30 
      6            +             +             +   
      7            +             +             +   

A minus sign means that, for spells of that level, improving spell skill 
to the indicated level will *never* change fail rate.  So, for example, 
Drain Life does not benefit from improving Attack school to Skilled, and 
Cure Sickness does not benefit from improving Healing school to Expert.

A plus sign means that improving the spell skill to the indicated level 
*can* improve fail rates for spells of that level.  This does not mean 
that improving the skill will *always* improve the fail rate; other 
spellcasting factors (robe, class, metal armor, etc) could peg failure 
rate at 0% or 100% or, rarely, some other value.

The fields with "XL" mean that at or above the given experience level, 
fail rates do not benefit from increasing skill to this level (same as 
minus sign above), and below it they can benefit (same as plus sign).




